<h2>Segment 240 &mdash; mind as the only creator</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s240S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p1">de ltar na</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p2">&#x27;gro ba ma lus pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p3">las las skyes par</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w1">gsungs</span> shing , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p4">sems spangs nas</span> ni <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p5">las kyang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w3">yod pa ma yin</span> te <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p6">sems dang bcas pa</span> kho nas <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w4">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w5">gsog pa</span>&#x27;i phyir na <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p7">las kyang sems la brten pa</span>&#x27;o, , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p8">de ltar na</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p9">sa bcu par</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w6">byed pa po</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w7">tshor ba po</span> med pa <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p10">zhes gsungs pa</span> la brten nas, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w8">tsam</span> gyi sgras <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p11">byed pa po gzhan &#x27;gog par bstan la</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s240S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p1">And so</span> it is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w1">spoken</span>, that <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p2">all the living beings of the universe</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p3">are produced by karma</span>. And if somehow you could <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p4">stop all minds</span>, then <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p5">karma itself</span> would <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w3">cease to be</span>, for it is only through <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p6">mind and what comes along with it</span> that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w4">karma</span> can be <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w5">collected</span>. Therefore <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p7">karma itself depends on the mind</span>. <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p8">So</span> the statement from the <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p9">Sutra of the Ten Levels</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p10">where it says</span> that there is no great <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w7">master</span> of all things, and no great <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w6">maker</span> of all things, conveys one meaning of the word <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s240w8">&quot;only&quot;</span> in the expression &quot;mind-only&quot;; <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s240p11">the point is that there is no other creator of things than the mind itself.</span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment proposed independently by Codex (English-first). The single med pa is omitted because its negation is distributed across GMR's two coordinated uses of no; this is not a null judgment. Modal and causal hinges remain unwrapped, and the final denial stays a depth-3 recast. C16:817 has identical ACIP, Wylie, and English; ILL:2687 offers a shorter comparative rendering of the same closing extent, without proving publication or ingestion lineage.</div>
